Package: PathMI
Type: Package
Title: Measuring Molecular Recoverability in Pathology Foundation-Model Embeddings
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sagnik", "Bhadury", email = "bhadury@umich.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Estimates how much information about a patient's binary
    molecular state the embeddings of a pathology foundation model carry
    (molecular recoverability) with PathMI, a Bayesian difference-of-entropies
    estimator: a Polya-Gamma logistic horseshoe ranks the coordinates, a walk
    over the nested models scored by their Laplace marginal likelihood selects
    the model, and the estimate is the log Bayes factor per patient. Around the
    estimator the package provides the metrology used in the accompanying
    paper: tile pooling and patient-level aggregation, linear and kernel PCA
    with out-of-sample projection, a permutation null with full refitting and
    joint-permutation max-T selection, half-sampling (delete-d jackknife)
    uncertainty, reproducibility bounds, attributable (incremental) and
    patient-held-out usable recoverability, patient-number learning curves
    with an evidence status, the exact tile-level decomposition with specific
    surprise maps, the tissue-sampling burden, the Recoverability Record with
    JSON export, simulators, and comparison estimators (LASSO-CV, OLS and the
    Donsker-Varadhan bound with a linear critic).
